 "issue": 229,
 "issue_title": "Validation has zero cross-parameter checks",
 "issue_body": "**File:** `src/validation.py:322-340,406-435,438-481`\n\n- `validate_parabolic_sag()` checks finiteness + `|sag|\u2264100` only. No `sag vs D` slope guard (`2\u00b7sag/r`), no `sag vs thickness` self-intersection check.\n- `validate_lens_parameters()` doesn't take `is_parabolic/sag` args.\n- `check_physical_feasibility()` only looks at `radius1/radius2` \u2014 `sag=100, D=2, thickness=0.1` sails through.\n\n**Fix:**\n```python\ndef validate_parabolic_sag(sag, diameter, thickness, ...):\n    r = diameter / 2\n    if abs(sag) > 0.75 * diameter: raise ...  # slope guard\n    if thickness + s1 - s2 <= 0: raise ...    # self-intersection\n    if thickness - s1 + s2 < min_edge: raise ...\n```",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/229",
 "pr": 241,
 "pr_title": "fix(validation): add parabolic-aware cross-parameter checks",
 "pr_body": "check_physical_feasibility() and validate_lens_parameters() now take is_parabolic_*/parabolic_sag_* args, probing through Lens so edge math stays vertex-correct (thickness - sag1 + sag2).\r\n\r\nAdd shared MIN_EDGE_THICKNESS soft floor for positive-but-fragile rims (replaces optimizer magic 0.5). Editor runs full feasibility for parabolic lenses too.\r\n\r\nTests: new parabolic impossible/feasible/thin-edge and editor warning coverage; full suite green, black clean.",
 "fix_commit": "cb051ebd5885ea6ac7771a4a8b2867e1198460e4",
